---
// Newsletter call-to-action band. The actual HubSpot form lives on /newsletter.
// Shown on the homepage, blog index, and the end of every blog post.
---

<section class="newsletter">
	<div class="newsletter-inner">
		<p class="eyebrow">The monthly edge</p>
		<h2>Sharper leadership, once a month.</h2>
		<p class="lede">
			Practical strategies for SME owners and directors: productivity, clarity and
			focus, performing in the room, better leadership, and the models, frameworks
			and AI ideas worth your time. No fluff, no spam, unsubscribe anytime.
		</p>
		<a href="/newsletter" class="btn-subscribe">Subscribe to the newsletter</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.newsletter {
		background: #111;
		color: #fff;
		padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.newsletter-inner {
		max-width: 640px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}
	.eyebrow {
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--accent);
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}
	.newsletter h2 {
		color: #fff;
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}
	.newsletter .lede {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: #d4d4d8;
		margin: 0 auto 2rem;
		max-width: 560px;
	}
	.btn-subscribe {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.85rem 2rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 1rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		border-radius: 4px;
		background: var(--accent);
		color: #fff;
		border: 2px solid var(--accent);
		transition: background 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
	}
	.btn-subscribe:hover {
		background: var(--accent-dark);
		border-color: var(--accent-dark);
	}
</style>
